sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch10-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The three kinds of geodetic on a cylinder (parallel rings, straight longitudinal lines and helical spirals) are all realised in the local wall thickenings of cylindrical plant cells and vessels, and the helical geodetic in the spiral coils of insect tracheae and tracheids.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Annular, longitudinal and spiral wall thickenings of plant cells are cylinder geodetics";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "geodesics on a cylinder of radius r: circles z = c, lines \\theta = c, helices z = a\\theta";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter X, “A Parenthetic Note on Geodetics”; topic “Geodetics of the cylinder”. Scope: plant xylem vessels and tracheids, insect tracheae"
}
